    "Ease": {
      "description": "How a key eases into the next one. linear, in (t^2), out (1-(1-t)^2) and step blend the two key states by the eased weight; smooth is a C1 cubic Hermite (Catmull-Rom) segment through the neighbouring keys: tangents are the finite differences across the previous and next key (wrapping for looping clips, zero at the ends of non-looping clips), angles in degrees on bone offsets, translations linear in value space, so velocity is continuous across keys. Scalar tracks follow the same rule. Looping clips drop a last key at or beyond the duration that repeats the first.",
      "enum": [
        "linear",
        "smooth",
        "in",
        "out",
        "step"
      ]
    },
